{"id":"moth","name":"Moth","aliases":["Moth"],"sources":["nave","torrey","easton"],"topics":["nave:moth","torrey:moth-the"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Moth","text":"Heb. ‘ash, from a root meaning “to fall away,” as moth-eaten garments fall to pieces (Job 4:19; 13:28; Isa. 50:9; 51:8; Hos. 5:12). Gr. ses, thus rendered in Matt. 6:19, 20; Luke 12:33. Allusion is thus made to the destruction of clothing by the larvae of the clothes-moth. This is the only lepidopterous insect referred to in Scripture."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H6211","lemma":"עָשׁ","xlit":"ʻâsh","gloss":"a moth","kjv":"moth. See also H5906","count":7,"share":0.7},{"strong":"H899","lemma":"בֶּגֶד","xlit":"beged","gloss":"a covering","kjv":"apparel, cloth, garment, lap","count":3,"share":0.3},{"strong":"H398","lemma":"אָכַל","xlit":"ʼâkal","gloss":"to eat","kjv":"at all, burn up, consume, devour","count":3,"share":0.3},{"strong":"H1004","lemma":"בַּיִת","xlit":"bayith","gloss":"a house","kjv":"court, daughter, door, dungeon","count":3,"share":0.3}],"verses":["Job.4.19","Job.13.28","Job.27.18","Ps.39.11","Isa.50.9","Isa.51.8","Hos.5.12","Matt.6.19","Matt.6.20","Jas.5.2"],"related":[{"id":"insects","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.061,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"life","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.021,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"houses","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.02,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"garments","type":"lexical","strong":"H899","why":"both lead with בֶּגֶד (H899)"},{"id":"huldah","type":"lexical","strong":"H899","why":"both lead with בֶּגֶד (H899)"},{"id":"mourning","type":"lexical","strong":"H899","why":"both lead with בֶּגֶד (H899)"},{"id":"rending","type":"lexical","strong":"H899","why":"both lead with בֶּגֶד (H899)"}],"works":[{"work":"anf02","title":"Ante-Nicene Fathers, Volume 2: Fathers of the Second Century","count":3,"chapters":[{"chapter":"ANFV.1","count":2,"book":"Fragments","ti